# Vue pages & components

- Always Composition API + `<script setup lang="ts">` + TypeScript.
- Keep business logic out of UI when possible; one responsibility per component.
- Reuse shells: `FormPanel`, `IndexPanel`, `Modal` / `ModalDelete`, `Loading`, `NotificationMessage`.
- Form controls: `components/inputs/` (`InputText`, `Select`, `LogoSelect`, `ColorSelect`, `ColorPicker`, etc.).
- Prefer `LogoSelect` for institution/network logos and `ColorSelect` for tags/categories/accounts (color swatch + label).
- Never call `fetch` or build HTTP/transform API payloads here — use `@/api/*` and transformers.

## Props & emits

```ts
interface Props {
  user: User;
  disabled?: boolean;
}

const props = defineProps<Props>();

const emit = defineEmits<{
  save: [user: User];
  cancel: [];
}>();
```

`withDefaults()` when optional props need defaults (see `FormPanel.vue`). Avoid runtime prop declarations unless required.

## State & templates

- Prefer `computed()` over watchers; `watch()` only for side effects.
- `ref()` for primitives/single values; `reactive()` for multi-field forms.
- Keep templates declarative; move non-trivial expressions to `computed()` or functions.
- Scoped styles; Bulma classes already used in the app. Inline styles only when dynamic.

## Loading

```ts
const loading = ref(false);

try {
  loading.value = true;
  // ...
} finally {
  loading.value = false;
}
```

List pages may use `showLoading` / `showTableLoading` (see `pages/tags/Index.vue`).

## Composables

No `composables/` folder yet. When extracting reusable non-UI logic, use `src/composables/useSomething.ts` (same spirit as stores/utils).
